body:
@lynicidn Are you saying you don’t think that this should be true for Arrayable objects?

``` php
$object->toArray([], [], $recursive) === ArrayHelper::toArray($object, [], $recursive)
```

(That test is true when $recursive = true, but not when $recursive = false.)

Maybe I’m missing something, but considering ArrayHelper::toArray() actually calls the Arrayable object’s toArray() method internally (if it is one), and considering that they both have “$recursive” arguments, expected behavior for me was that they would both behave the same when $recursive = false.

Currently I’m doing the following workaround (until my patch makes it in):

``` php
if ($object instanceof Arrayable) {
    $arr = $object->toArray([], [], false);
} else {
    $arr = ArrayHelper::toArray($object, [], false);
}
```

I certainly hope I can simplify that to this line when Yii 2.0.4 comes out:

``` php
$arr = ArrayHelper::toArray($object, [], false);
```

@lynicidn [As I said when you pointed out the same line in the commit comment](https://github.com/brandonkelly/yii2/commit/ef8925618f316d7324cd7898f006163550b8e2af#commitcomment-10283075), the problem is, by the time line 96 is executed, the damage described here has already been done:
https://github.com/yiisoft/yii2/blob/befd42f46ad324e003be30fa2e5cbfd760d05bad/framework/helpers/BaseArrayHelper.php#L87-L88

To clarify, because $recursive isn’t passed to the Arrayable object’s toArray() method, toArray() will end up recursively turning all nested items into arrays (such as nested DateTime properties, as in the example I gave above). So by the time line 96 is called, it doesn't matter if $recursive is false anymore - everything has already been recursively turned into an array at that point.

Post4 doesn't implement yii\base\Arrayable, so that’s not a valid test. And the $properties argument you're passing into ArrayHelper::toArray() in the first assertion isn’t even a [supported format](http://www.yiiframework.com/doc-2.0/yii-helpers-basearrayhelper.html#toArray%28%29-detail).

Here:

``` php
use yii\base\Object;
use yii\base\Arrayable;
use yii\base\ArrayableTrait;
use yii\helpers\ArrayHelper;

class Post3 extends Object
{
    // ...
}

class Post4 extends Object implements Arrayable
{
    use ArrayableTrait;

    public $id = 55;
    public $subObject;

    public function init()
    {
        $this->subObject = new Post3();
    }
}
```

``` php
$object = new Post4();

$this->assertEquals(
    ['id' => 55, 'subObject' => $object->subObject],
    ArrayHelper::toArray($object, [], false)
);
```
